Cyre was the cultural heart of pre-war Galifar — renowned for art, craftsmanship, and arcane innovation. On Olarune 20, 994 YK (the Day of Mourning), Cyre was destroyed by an unknown magical catastrophe and became [[The Mournland]].

!! Pre-War Cyre
Considered the most culturally refined of the Five Nations. Its capital, Metrol, housed some of Khorvaire's greatest museums, theaters, and magical academies. Cyre hosted major [[House Cannith]] manufacturing facilities, including creation forges that produced the bulk of [[Warforged]] soldiers during the [[Last War]].

!! The Day of Mourning
On Olarune 20, 994 YK, a grey mist rolled outward from somewhere in Cyre's interior and killed or transformed everything it touched. When the mist settled, all living Cyrans within the borders were dead or gone. The cause remains one of Khorvaire's greatest unsolved mysteries. Leading theories: a Cannith or Aundairian weapon, a planar collapse into Mabar or Xoriat, or collective magical backlash from the Last War.

!! The Cyran Diaspora
Cyrans who were outside their borders when the Mourning struck — soldiers, diplomats, travelers — became refugees under the Treaty of Thronehold. The settlement of New Cyre in Breland hosts the largest concentration but is not a recognized nation. Cyrans carry a collective grief that makes them a distinct cultural and political force.

